{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Strength</b> — as though she clothes herself in strength and splendor." "<b>For the last day</b> — at the time of her old age she is able to stand laughing, and she does not fear lack, or for the world to come." "<b>Kindness</b> — that she is prepared to perform kindness."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:52.717273875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}